course: dictionary
lesson: 4243
title: Granite: a hard rock and a hard word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Granite is the name of a rock, and it can also describe something very firm. «People have always built with local stone, so old towns often show the local geology, like the granite of Aberdeen.» Here granite is the stone the buildings are made from.
explain: Granite is a very hard, grey, pink or speckled rock. It formed from hot liquid rock that cooled slowly deep under the ground. «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica, formed deep underground.» The speckles are crystals you can see with a magnifying glass.
explain: The second meaning is about firmness. If a rule or a promise is made of granite, it is very firm and nobody can easily change it. Use the words around granite to decide which meaning fits, and try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Granite is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some granite, not a granite.
fact: Granite is an igneous rock: it forms when hot liquid rock cools slowly underground.
fact: The big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica are the speckles you can see in granite.
fact: Granite is hard and does not soak up water, so it is used for kitchen worktops, buildings and gravestones.
fact: «Granite is seen at the surface only after the rocks above it have been worn away, as on Dartmoor in England.»
exercise: What kind of rock is granite? | *A very hard rock that formed from hot liquid rock cooling underground | A soft rock that soaks up water like a sponge | A metal found in rivers | A type of sand from the beach
exercise: «Her promise was made of granite, and nobody could change it.» What does granite suggest here? | Cold and wet | Soft and easy to bend | *Very firm and hard to change | Bright and shiny
exercise: Find and copy one mineral named in «Granite is a speckled igneous rock with big crystals of quartz, feldspar and mica.» | *quartz | igneous | rock | speckled
test: Why is granite used for kitchen worktops? | It melts easily in the heat | It is cheap and light | *It is hard and does not soak up water | It is soft and bends
test: «Granite is seen at the surface only after the rocks above it have been worn away.» What must happen before granite can be seen at the surface? | It must be dug up and buried again | Someone must paint it grey | *The rocks above it must be worn away | The sea must freeze over it
exam: Which sentence uses granite in the second, figurative meaning? | *«Her decision was granite, and no argument could shift it.» | «Granite is a mix of quartz, feldspar and mica.» | «The granite was grey and speckled.» | «The old castle was built of granite.»
